<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humphrey II of Toron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1179</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Humphrey II of Toron was lord of Toron and constable of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> from 1152. He was trusted as a negotiator by Muslim rulers, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, and fought in many campaigns. He was mortally wounded in 1179 covering King Baldwin IV's retreat after the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banias">Banias</a>. His grandson Humphrey IV married Isabella, heir to the throne.</p></div>
